[{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"CurrentModule = DynamicStructs","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Dynamic-Structs","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Dynamic structs in DynamicStructs.jl extend Julia's standard structs with the ability to add, modify, and delete properties at runtime. This provides flexibility similar to what you might find in dynamic languages while maintaining the type safety and performance benefits of Julia's standard structs.","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"See Performance for details on performance characteristics and optimization tips, and Utilities for utilities to work with dynamic properties.","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"@dynamic\nisdynamictype\nisdynamic","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#DynamicStructs.@dynamic","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"DynamicStructs.@dynamic","text":"@dynamic [mutable] struct ... end\n\nDefine a dynamic struct:\n\nInstances of dynamic structs have dynamic properties that can be added/deleted at runtime. These properties are similar to Any-typed fields of structs in terms of performance.\nFields remain statically typed and accessing them compiles similarly to structs, so performance should not be significantly affected.\nThe macro adds a hidden field for storing dynamic properties with lazy initialization, meaning that the underlying storage is not allocated until the first dynamic property is added.\nThe default constructors of dynamic structs accept keyword arguments for dynamic properties, with a Base.show method that reflects this. These are only present if the block is free of any non-field expressions, such as custom constructors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"},{"location":"dynamic/#DynamicStructs.isdynamictype","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"DynamicStructs.isdynamictype","text":"isdynamictype(T)\n\nCheck if T is a dynamic type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"dynamic/#DynamicStructs.isdynamic","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"DynamicStructs.isdynamic","text":"isdynamic(x)\n\nCheck if x is an instance of a dynamic type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"dynamic/#Core-Concepts","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Core Concepts","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Dynamic structs combine static fields with dynamically added properties:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Static fields: Defined at compile time, type-stable, and efficient\nDynamic properties: Added at runtime, perform like Any-typed fields","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Creating-Dynamic-Structs","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Creating Dynamic Structs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Use the @dynamic macro to create a dynamic struct:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"using DynamicStructs\n\n@dynamic struct GPU\n    model::String\n    year::Int\nend\n\ngpu = GPU(\"RTX 6000 Ada\", 2022, hourly_cost = 0.18)","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"You can also create mutable dynamic structs:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"@dynamic mutable struct Person\n    name::String\n    age::Int\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Working-with-Dynamic-Properties","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Working with Dynamic Properties","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/#Adding-and-Accessing-Properties","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Adding and Accessing Properties","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"p = Person(\"Bob\", 25, hobby=\"Reading\", location=\"New York\")\n\np.skills = [\"Programming\", \"Design\"];\n\np.name    # Static field\np.hobby   # Dynamic property","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Modifying-Properties","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Modifying Properties","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"p.hobby = \"Gaming\"\n\np.age = 26\n\np","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Removing-Properties","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Removing Properties","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"delete!(p, :hobby)\n\nhasproperty(p, :hobby)","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Reflection","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Reflection","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Check if a type is dynamic or if an instance is of a dynamic type:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"isdynamictype(Person)\nisdynamic(p)","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Implementation-Details","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Implementation Details","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Dynamic structs include a private __properties field that stores all dynamic properties in a dictionary-like structure. This field is lazily initialized, meaning no storage is allocated until the first dynamic property is added.","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"The default constructors of dynamic structs accept keyword arguments for dynamic properties, and a custom Base.show method provides a clean representation.","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/#Overwriting-dynamic-methods","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Overwriting dynamic methods","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"The @dynamic macro defines methods for the following functions:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Base.hasproperty\nBase.propertynames\nBase.getproperty\nBase.setproperty!\nBase.delete!\nBase.hash\nBase.:(==)","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"This prevents you from defining your own methods without disabling file precompilation (through __precompile__(false)).","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Each of the functions above redirect to their respective generic functions in DynamicStructs:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"DynamicStructs.dynamic_hasproperty\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_propertynames\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_getproperty\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_setproperty!\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_delete!\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_hash\nDynamicStructs.dynamic_equality","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"These are specifically defined for dynamic structs, and should be used to inherit the default behaviors.","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"Let us demonstrate with a silly example:","category":"page"},{"location":"dynamic/","page":"Dynamic Structs","title":"Dynamic Structs","text":"__precompile__(false) # put in same file\n\n@dynamic struct AddOne end\n\nfunction Base.getproperty(x::AddOne, name::Symbol)\n    DynamicStructs.dynamic_getproperty(x, name) + 1\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"CurrentModule = DynamicStructs","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/#Performance","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/#Static-fields","page":"Performance","title":"Static fields","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"A comparison between accessing static fields of regular and dynamic structs shows that performance impact is minimal, and the LLVM code of accessing fields of a dynamic struct is still \"nice\".","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"using DynamicStructs, Chairmarks, InteractiveUtils\n\nstruct A\n    x::Int\nend\n\n@dynamic struct B\n    x::Int\nend\n\na, b = A(1), B(1)\n\nf(arg) = arg.x^2\n\n@b f($a)\n\n@b f($b)\n\n@code_llvm f(a)\n\n@code_llvm f(b)","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/#Dynamic-properties","page":"Performance","title":"Dynamic properties","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"Dynamic structs build on the static fields of regular structs, essentially strapping on an AbstractDict{Symbol,Any}, which gets accessed if the property is not a field. This flexibility makes for a convenient interface, but is also inherently type-unstable, meaning they will perform similarly to a field of unspecified type. The LLVM code generated from dynamic property access is however significantly longer.","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"struct C\n    x::Int\n    y\nend\n\nb, c = B(1, y=2), b(1, 2);\n\ng(arg) = arg.y^2;\n\n@b g($b)\n\n@b g($c)","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/#Tips","page":"Performance","title":"Tips","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/#Type-assertions-for-type-stability-and-improved-performance","page":"Performance","title":"Type assertions for type stability and improved performance","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"v = [B(i, y=i) for i in 1:100];\n\n@b sum(b.x for b in $v)\n\n@b sum(b.y for b in $v)\n\n@b sum(b.y::Int for b in $v)","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/#Function-barriers-help...-sometimes","page":"Performance","title":"Function barriers help... sometimes","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"We observe that in one scenario, broadcasted addition of short vectors is 2x faster with a function barrier, but 2x slower for longer vectors. This happens also with Any-typed fields of regular structs.","category":"page"},{"location":"performance/","page":"Performance","title":"Performance","text":"@dynamic struct D end\n\nf(a, b) = a.x .+ a.x;\n\ng(x1, x2) = x1 .+ x2;\n\nf_barrier(a, b) = g(a.x, b.x);\n\na, b = D(x = rand(1)), D(x = rand(1));\n\n@b f($a, $b)\n\n@b f_barrier($a, $b)\n\na, b = D(x = rand(10000)), D(x = rand(10000));\n\n@b f($a, $b)\n\n@b f_barrier($a, $b)","category":"page"},{"location":"utilities/","page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","text":"CurrentModule = DynamicStructs","category":"page"},{"location":"utilities/#Utilities","page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"utilities/","page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","text":"DynamicStructs defines a few functions to simplify working with dynamic properties, as well as the more general case where propertynames(x) != fieldnames(typeof(x)).","category":"page"},{"location":"utilities/","page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","text":"NoFields\nOnlyFields\nBase.propertynames\npropertyvalues\npropertypairs","category":"page"},{"location":"utilities/#DynamicStructs.NoFields","page":"Utilities","title":"DynamicStructs.NoFields","text":"Insert as second argument to Base.propertynames, propertyvalues, or propertypairs to exclude field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"utilities/#DynamicStructs.OnlyFields","page":"Utilities","title":"DynamicStructs.OnlyFields","text":"Insert as second argument to Base.propertynames, propertyvalues, or propertypairs to include only field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"utilities/#Base.propertynames","page":"Utilities","title":"Base.propertynames","text":"Base.propertynames(x, ::Type{NoFields}, private=false)\n\nExcludes field names.\n\n\n\n\n\nBase.propertynames(x, ::Type{OnlyFields}, private=false)\n\nIncludes only field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"utilities/#DynamicStructs.propertyvalues","page":"Utilities","title":"DynamicStructs.propertyvalues","text":"propertyvalues(x, args...)\n\nGet a tuple of the current property values. args is propagated to Base.propertynames.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"utilities/#DynamicStructs.propertypairs","page":"Utilities","title":"DynamicStructs.propertypairs","text":"propertypairs(x, args...)\n\nGet a tuple of the current property names and values. args is propagated to Base.propertynames.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"utilities/#Examples","page":"Utilities","title":"Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"utilities/","page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","text":"using DynamicStructs\n\n@dynamic struct Spaceship\n    name::String\nend\n\nship = Spaceship(\"Blip-A\"; pressure=28.0)\n\npropertynames(ship, OnlyFields)\n\npropertynames(ship, NoFields)\n\npropertyvalues(ship)\n\npropertyvalues(ship, NoFields)\n\npropertypairs(ship)\n\npropertypairs(ship, OnlyFields)\n\npropertypairs(ship, true) # shows all properties, including private","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"CurrentModule = DynamicStructs","category":"page"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for DynamicStructs.","category":"page"},{"location":"#Installation","page":"Home","title":"Installation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"using Pkg\npkg\"add DynamicStructs\"","category":"page"},{"location":"#Index","page":"Home","title":"Index","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"}]
